      "claim": "The query is adamantan-1-amine, a small rigid primary amine (MW 151, TPSA 26, no rotatable bonds, fully protonated at physiological pH); no direct amantadine-specific F record is supplied, so the decision remains transfer-based.",
      "card_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 provides direct intestinal absorption evidence for small polar molecules: gabapentin human fraction absorbed 74% (C142) and rat Fa 80–98% (C132, C150, C156), despite low Caco-2 permeability (C128), showing that low monolayer permeability does not preclude high absorption for small polar molecules.",
      "card_ids": ["C128","C132","C142","C150","C156"]
    },
